"Let $p$ be a prime and let $A,B$ be non-empty subsets of $\\mathbb{F}_p$. For subsets $A,B\\subset\\mathbb{F}_p$, write $A+B=\\{a+b\\mid a\\in A,\\ b\\in B\\}$ and define the **restricted sumset** $A\\dot{+}B=\\{a+b\\mid a\\in A,\\ b\\in B,\\ a\\neq b\\}$. **Erdős–Heilbronn conjecture.** For every $A\\subset\\mathbb{F}_p$, \n\n$$\n|A\\dot{+}A|\\geqslant\\min\\left\\{p,2|A|-3\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe conjecture concerns the restricted analogue of the Cauchy–Davenport theorem and was later proved, so the database status is recorded as solved."